/bin/
/obj/
/benchmark-results/

# alr's private working-state cache, not source: alire.lock pins "system"
# origins (e.g. libgmp) to the resolving platform's package manager and
# name, which does not carry over between macOS and Linux -- see the CI
# workflow's git history for the Ubuntu breakage this caused when it was
# committed. build_hash_inputs/settings.toml/flags/ are per-machine build
# state, and alire.toml.prev has even been caught holding a stale manifest
# from an unrelated crate. None of it belongs in version control; the real
# manifest is the top-level alire.toml, outside this directory.
/alire/

# Same reasoning: these are alr-generated config mirrors (host OS/arch/distro
# baked in at resolve time) written to both the project root and config/.
# Committing them caused the exact cross-platform breakage described above,
# this time for Alire_Host_OS/Arch/Distro on a Linux deployment.
/adalang_analyzer_config.gpr
/adalang_analyzer_config.ads
/adalang_analyzer_config.h
/config/adalang_analyzer_config.gpr
/config/adalang_analyzer_config.ads
/config/adalang_analyzer_config.h

/CLAUDE.md
